   "table": "",
   "description": "Box plots compare sovereign asset shares for central banks and domestic banks and the share of total debt held by domestic nonbanks in 2000–14 and 2015–24. Central banks have the highest medians and upper whiskers in both periods. Median shares rise for domestic banks and nonbanks in the later period; the lowest median is for domestic nonbanks in 2000–14.",
   "notes": "Sources: Original calculations based on data from Arslanalp and Tsuda 2014 and the International Monetary Fund’s International Financial Statistics database. Notes: For central bank and domestic banks, sovereign assets is the sum of claims on the central government, local government, and public nonfinancial corporations. Domestic nonbanks’ holdings of sovereign assets come from Arslanalp and Tsuda (2014). The distributions of the relevant indicator are over two periods: 2000–14 and 2015–24 for the sample of countries that use the Debt Sustainability Framework for Low-Income Countries. Each box represents the 25th (Q1) to 75th (Q3) percentile range, the line inside the box is the median, the X mark is the mean, and the bottom and top whiskers are the 1.5 × IQR from Q1 and Q3, respectively. IDA = International Development Association; IQR = interquartile range."
